  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Pennsylvania State University has $402M in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. Pennsylvania State University won 226 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $1.8M, and obligations are up 16.5% year over year. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer, obligating $397M to Pennsylvania State University. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) is the largest market, attracting $399M in obligations. Pennsylvania State University has trended upward over recent fiscal years: FY21 $202M, FY22 $256M, FY23 $314M, FY24 $331M, FY25 $345M, and FY26 $402M. Current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date obligations. The dataset also lists smaller obligations from the Department of the Interior $3M and the National Aeronautics and Space Administration $2.4M, and shows minor negative or zero entries in a few markets and agencies, reflecting adjustments or accounting entries in FY2026 to date.",
