        "body": "The Department of Defense is the primary source of federal obligations for Pennsylvania State University, with $397M obligated in FY2026 to date. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) is the main market, with $399M in obligations. Pennsylvania State University has shown steady growth in obligations over recent fiscal years, rising from $202M in FY21 to $402M in FY26. The overall program so far includes 226 awards with an average award size of $1.8M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who buys the most from Pennsylvania State University and what do they buy?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the top buying agency for Pennsylvania State University at $397M in FY2026 to date. The National Aeronautics and Space Administration bought $2.4M and the Department of the Interior bought $3M in the same period. Pennsylvania State University sells primarily research and development services, led by Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) at $399M, with smaller obligations in other research and education-related NAICS categories."
